#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# scorer_gi_prime

#% text
# `scorer_gi_prime(z)` gives the derivative of the Scorer function `Gi(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `Gi'(z) = Bi'(z) - Hi'(z)` (DLMF 9.12); `Gi'(0) = Bi'(0)/3`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
scorer_gi_prime(1.0)
#% output
#= -0.04843777526150429

#% cell
n(scorer_gi_prime(2), 30)
#% output
#= -0.06725379415890528611444655157876688

#% cell
scorer_gi_prime(0)
#% output
#= 3^(1/6)/(3*gamma(1/3))

#% text
# A difference quotient of `scorer_gi`:

#% cell
(scorer_gi(1.0 + 1.0e-6) - scorer_gi(1.0 - 1.0e-6))/2.0e-6
#% output
#= -0.04843777526297721

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `scorer_gi`, `scorer_hi_prime`, `airy_bi_prime`
